meta {
  name: 30-Leave a 5-star review
  type: http
  seq: 30
}

post {
  url: {{host}}/api/listings/1/reviews
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{temi_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "revieweeUserId": 1,
    "rating": 5,
    "body": "First place I ever rented and the owner was amazing — answered every silly question, didn't push me on the price, gave me till month-end to move in. The flat is exactly what the photos showed. Would 100% rent from again."
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: in [201, 400, 401, 403, 404, 409]
}

docs {
  Two weeks after move-in. Closing the loop with a 5-star review.

  Two things bother me about this endpoint:
  1. I have to know the revieweeUserId — I have to remember /
     re-fetch the listing detail to get the ownerId. The platform
     could just default the reviewee to "the other party of the
     accepted offer" without me having to specify.
  2. There's no field for "reviewing the agent vs the owner" — if
     I'd dealt with both, I'd want to leave separate ratings. The
     persona doc hints at this but the schema doesn't.
}
